<title>JAPAN: NatWest to join Tokyo Stock Exchange in January.</title>
<headline>NatWest to join Tokyo Stock Exchange in January.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) said on Tuesday that NatWest Securities Japan Ltd will become a member of the exchange on January 6.</p>
<p>NatWest Securities, a unit of Britain's National Westminster Bank Plc, has purchased a TSE membership from Citicorp International Securities Ltd, a unit of New York-based Citicorp, the TSE said.</p>
<p>The Citicorp unit said in August that it planned to pull out of Japan's equity markets.</p>
<p>NatWest Securities previously held a TSE membership but sold it in April 1993 and halted securities transactions in Japan except for bond trading.</p>
</text>
